    },
    {
      "source_number": "228",
      "task": "Use each two-term specification to determine every requested term; a requests c_7,c_5,c_10, not a consecutive triple.",
      "solution": "a: 22-16=2d, so d=3. c_7=16+3=19; c_5=16-3=13; c_10=16+4*3=28. b: 8-18=2d, so d=-5. c_12=18-5=13; c_9=18+(-2)*(-5)=28; c_14=18+3*(-5)=3.",
      "distinction": "Infer a per-step difference, then move by signed index distances for the intermediate, earlier, and later requested terms."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "229",
      "task": "Prove that some angle is 60 degrees for an arbitrary triangle whose three angle measures form an arithmetic sequence.",
      "solution": "Let alpha,beta,gamma be the three measures in the stated arithmetic-sequence order. Equal successive differences imply 2beta=alpha+gamma, so beta=(alpha+gamma)/2. The triangle angle sum is alpha+beta+gamma=180 degrees. Substituting alpha+gamma=2beta yields 3beta=180 degrees, hence beta=60 degrees. No assertion that all three angles are equal is needed.",
      "distinction": "The arithmetic-mean property and the triangle angle sum jointly establish the conclusion; either alone or a single example is insufficient."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "230",
      "task": "Find the middle side length, retaining both the perimeter and the arithmetic-sequence condition.",
      "solution": "Write the ordered side lengths p,q,r in cm. Arithmetic progression gives p+r=2q. Perimeter gives p+q+r=24, thus 3q=24 and q=8 cm. The outer lengths are not individually determined and need not equal q; a valid example is 6,8,10.",
      "distinction": "The middle member is the mean of the two outer members, not half the perimeter or necessarily a side of an equilateral triangle."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "231",
      "task": "Simplify the exponents and evaluate both independent expressions at their full scientific-notation substitutions.",
      "solution": "a: coefficients multiply to 8; a exponent is 3+(-4)=-1 and b exponent is -5+4=-1. Expression=8/(ab), with nonzero a,b. At a=6400 and b=1/40, ab=160 and value=8/160=1/20=0.05. b: the squared factor is (1/9)a^(-2)b^4; multiplying by 9a^3b^(-5) gives a/b. At a=370 and b=17/100, value=37000/17, approximately 2176.470588. Use the exact rational value rather than undocumented rounding.",
